# InterfaceOverrides

**Namespace**: `Cyrena.Options`
**Assembly**: `Cyrena.Components.Core`

```csharp
public sealed class InterfaceOverrides
{
    private Type? _fileAttacher { get; set; }

    public void UseFileAttacher<TFileAttacher>()
        where TFileAttacher : class, IFileAttacher;

    public Type? FileAttacher => _fileAttacher;
}
```

Used to change the default components used in the chat interface. Kernel-locked.

## Members

### `UseFileAttacher<TFileAttacher>()`
Records `typeof(TFileAttacher)` as the implementation of `IFileAttacher` to use. The constraint is `class, IFileAttacher` (so the type must be a reference type implementing the contract).

### `FileAttacher`
Read-only property exposing the currently selected file-attacher `Type`, or `null` if none was selected. The chat UI consults this to decide which component to render.

## Usage

Resolve `InterfaceOverrides` from the kernel scope and call `UseFileAttacher<T>` inside `IAssistantMode.ConfigureAsync`:

```csharp
public class MyMode : IAssistantMode
{
    public string Id => "my-mode";

    public Task ConfigureAsync(CyrenaKernelBuilder builder)
    {
        var overrides = builder.Services.BuildServiceProvider()
            .GetRequiredService<InterfaceOverrides>();
        overrides.UseFileAttacher<MyCustomAttacher>();
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }
}
```

Or, more idiomatically, inside a plugin:

```csharp
public class MyPlugin : IAssistantPlugin
{
    public Task LoadAsync(CyrenaKernelBuilder builder)
    {
        var overrides = builder.GetFeatureOption<InterfaceOverrides>();
        overrides.UseFileAttacher<MyCustomAttacher>();
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }
}
```

## Extensibility
The class is `sealed` and currently only exposes the `FileAttacher` override. New override hooks should be added here as Cyréna grows.

## Related
